# Deferred DB-Hardening Tasks

When touching these features, implement the matching hardening — DB constraints alone are not enough.

## 1. Checkout / Order Service

### 1.1 Inventory race — pessimistic lock

Inside `DB::transaction`, before changing `reserved_quantity`:

```php
$inventory = Inventory::where('book_id', $item->book_id)
    ->lockForUpdate()
    ->first();
```

Verify available stock, then `increment('reserved_quantity', ...)`. The CHECK `reserved_quantity <= quantity` is a safety net only.

### 1.2 PromotionItem `sold_quantity`

When incrementing `sold_quantity`, `lockForUpdate()` the `promotion_items` row and ensure `sold_quantity + qty <= stock_limit` when `stock_limit` is set.

### 1.3 Order line snapshots

`order_items.price`, `total_price`, `discount_amount` must be populated from server-side prices at checkout time (never trust client). If audit needs title/SKU at order time, add `book_name_snapshot` / `book_sku_snapshot` via a new migration.

## 2. VietQR / gateway payments

### 2.1 Use `payment_transactions`

Schema exists (`payment_transactions` migration). Add `App\Models\PaymentTransaction`, write a row per charge attempt / webhook / refund. Use composite unique `(gateway, gateway_txn_id)` for idempotency (nullable `gateway_txn_id` allowed for pending COD-like flows).

### 2.2 Order payment status

Update `orders.payment_status` only after persisting the matching transaction row(s), not from raw webhook alone.

## 3. Customer-facing Review API

### 3.1 Use Eloquent only

Create/update/delete reviews through Eloquent so `ReviewObserver` keeps `books.review_count` and `books.average_rating` in sync. Avoid `DB::table('reviews')` for mutations.

### 3.2 Approved-only aggregates

Any manual aggregation must filter `status = ReviewStatus::APPROVED`, consistent with `ReviewObserver`.

## 4. Review images (removed until needed)

`Review::images()` was removed — no `review_images` table. When product requires photo reviews:

- Migration `review_images` (mirror `book_images`: `review_id`, `public_id`, `image_url`, `sort_order`).
- Model `ReviewImage` and restore `Review::images()` HasMany.
- Cloudinary cleanup on delete (pattern: `BookImageObserver` / `BookObserver`).
